  id: W3_05
  era: "c. 1590\u20131595"
  title: A page from the Akbarnama
  text: A page from the Akbarnama. The Akbarnama, 'Book of Akbar', is the official history of the third Mughal emperor, written by his minister Abul Fazl. Teams of court artists illustrated it with vivid scenes of battles, hunts and court life, blending Persian, Indian and European ideas into a new Mughal style. Akbar could not read, but he loved books. He held debates between scholars of many faiths and promoted a policy of sulh-i kul, 'peace with all'.
